<title>USA: Jefferson sees earnings hurt by low prices.</title>
<headline>Jefferson sees earnings hurt by low prices.</headline>
<dateline>CLAYTON, Mo. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jefferson Smurfit Corp said it expects product prices to remain low through the early months of 1997 and to &quot;negatively affect earnings.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;However, industry inventories in containerboard and newsprint have declined steadily in the past few months, while the rate of growth of new containerboard capacity has moderated,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;Given continued economic expansion, we could see a recovery in the company's principal markets during the second half of 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
